{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghB9Wzg6kTnQvJNbVbgd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019dTpDS7RMe6A151z2dJdLw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202613__x53986f/work/EyeOf*/ && sed -n 120,400p hub/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2834,"cache_read_input_tokens":82198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2834},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"fec0f96f-aa7c-4792-b844-aa2c585412bd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:26:45.551Z","request_id":"req_011CghB9WjZ1M4JXFEqxRDFg","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019dTpDS7RMe6A151z2dJdLw":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202613__x53986f/work/EyeOf*/ && sed -n 120,400p hub/README.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019dTpDS7RMe6A151z2dJdLw","type":"tool_result","content":"`info` (also on `AIHub` after `connect()`):\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `me` | this copy's player id |\n| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\n| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n| `seed` | a number, the same on every copy, behind `AIHub.rng(label)` |\n\nNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\nfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n\n### The card\n\nBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\nnext and say when they are ready. By default the hub shows its own card over\nthe game. A game can make the card its own, as part of the game:\n\n```js\nAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n```\n\nThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\nscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\ntitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\nit deserves.\n\nWhile it is on, the card shows:\n\n- the game's name;\n- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n- how to win the round;\n- the controls this player will use;\n- the time left, from the `card` event.\n\nAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\non the card:\n\n- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n\nNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\nchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\nnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n\n`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n\n### The start\n\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n`start`.\n\n### Reporting\n\n- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n  by the host only:\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n    placed last.\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n\n### Time-up and the end\n\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n  `finish()` by then is void.\n- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n  game, then removes it.\n\n| `end` reason | |\n|---|---|\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n\n### Leaving\n\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\n  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n  that player leaving.\n\n### Scoring\n\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\n  progress.\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n  result instead of medals.\n- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\n\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\nresults:\n\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n\nPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n\n---\n\n## Sending data between copies\n\n### Parallel\n\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n\n### Ghost\n\nEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\nthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\nonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\ncharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n\n### Shared world\n\n- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n  every copy.\n\n### `send()` and `message`\n\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n  client drops the rest.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\nIn a session:\n\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n\n| Tag | |\n|---|---|\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n\n### API\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"a41e7f8c-4f91-4ffb-ae55-ad55e337ee01","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:26:45.577Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"`info` (also on `AIHub` after `connect()`):\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `me` | this copy's player id |\n| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\n| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n| `seed` | a number, the same on every copy, behind `AIHub.rng(label)` |\n\nNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\nfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n\n### The card\n\nBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\nnext and say when they are ready. By default the hub shows its own card over\nthe game. A game can make the card its own, as part of the game:\n\n```js\nAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n```\n\nThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\nscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\ntitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\nit deserves.\n\nWhile it is on, the card shows:\n\n- the game's name;\n- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n- how to win the round;\n- the controls this player will use;\n- the time left, from the `card` event.\n\nAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\non the card:\n\n- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n\nNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\nchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\nnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n\n`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n\n### The start\n\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n`start`.\n\n### Reporting\n\n- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n  by the host only:\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n    placed last.\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n\n### Time-up and the end\n\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n  `finish()` by then is void.\n- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n  game, then removes it.\n\n| `end` reason | |\n|---|---|\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n\n### Leaving\n\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\n  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n  that player leaving.\n\n### Scoring\n\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\n  progress.\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n  result instead of medals.\n- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\n\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\nresults:\n\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n\nPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n\n---\n\n## Sending data between copies\n\n### Parallel\n\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n\n### Ghost\n\nEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\nthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\nonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\ncharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n\n### Shared world\n\n- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n  every copy.\n\n### `send()` and `message`\n\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n  client drops the rest.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\nIn a session:\n\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n\n| Tag | |\n|---|---|\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n\n### API\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019dTpDS7RMe6A151z2dJdLw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghB9Wzg6kTnQvJNbVbgd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014U3hsAsGpjfutDyVbmeHBR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202613__x53986f/work/EyeOf*/ && cat _ref/engine-src/src/starter3d/00-shell.js && cat _ref/engine-src/src/starter3d/70-crawler.js"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2834,"cache_read_input_tokens":82198,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2834},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"623d5f65-f383-4563-8836-b6ab6bf1ece3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:26:46.041Z","request_id":"req_011CghB9WjZ1M4JXFEqxRDFg","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014U3hsAsGpjfutDyVbmeHBR":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202613__x53986f/work/EyeOf*/ && cat _ref/engine-src/src/starter3d/00-shell.js && cat _ref/engine-src/src/starter3d/70-crawler.js"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014U3hsAsGpjfutDyVbmeHBR","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (52.9KB). Full output saved to: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-build--20261103-202613--x53986f-work/6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a/tool-results/bth090424.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE 3D STARTER: a title menu and the 3D slices (a 3D genre kit file holds one). Each slice is a complete small\n * 3D game, written to be copied and changed: its own header (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch\n * controls, its deep links and how it works. The 3D engine's manual (the header of engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js) says how a\n * game runs on a 3D world: E.Game as in 2D with bg: null, world.step(dt) in update, world.draw(r) then the HUD in draw.\n * THE SHELL'S KEYS: M mutes; in a slice whose camera follows the game's view, V changes the view, [ ] turn it and 0\n * resets it (the wheel, - and = zoom where the scene allows); the pause menu's Display has the 3D settings\n * (characters as cards or puppets, the picture's resolution, shadows).\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, the boot steps) stays unless you replace\n * it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\nconst E = My3D2dge, W3 = E.World3D, { clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes, each slice with its own world ----\n * bg: null keeps the game's canvas clear over the 3D picture; E.World3D.INPUT: WASD move, Space jump, J or a click\n * attack, Shift dash, E skill, C camera; E.World3D.SETTINGS: the 3D settings in the pause menu */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: W3.INPUT, menu: { settings: W3.SETTINGS } });\nconst P = game.particles, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {}, BOOT = [];    // BOOT: the slices' heavy setup, [label, fn] steps run behind the boot screen\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"468ce631-3aeb-4035-8164-73939d52e6c9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:26:46.074Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE 3D STARTER: a title menu and the 3D slices (a 3D genre kit file holds one). Each slice is a complete small\n * 3D game, written to be copied and changed: its own header (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch\n * controls, its deep links and how it works. The 3D engine's manual (the header of engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js) says how a\n * game runs on a 3D world: E.Game as in 2D with bg: null, world.step(dt) in update, world.draw(r) then the HUD in draw.\n * THE SHELL'S KEYS: M mutes; in a slice whose camera follows the game's view, V changes the view, [ ] turn it and 0\n * resets it (the wheel, - and = zoom where the scene allows); the pause menu's Display has the 3D settings\n * (characters as cards or puppets, the picture's resolution, shadows).\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, the boot steps) stays unless you replace\n * it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\nconst E = My3D2dge, W3 = E.World3D, { clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes, each slice with its own world ----\n * bg: null keeps the game's canvas clear over the 3D picture; E.World3D.INPUT: WASD move, Space jump, J or a click\n * attack, Shift dash, E skill, C camera; E.World3D.SETTINGS: the 3D settings in the pause menu */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: W3.INPUT, menu: { settings: W3.SETTINGS } });\nconst P = game.particles, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {}, BOOT = [];    // BOOT: the slices' heavy setup, [label, fn] steps run behind the boot screen\n// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\nconst SLICES = [\n  { id: 'action', label: 'ACTION', about: 'A 3D ARENA: COMBOS, DASHES AND WAVES', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'A 3D COURSE: ISLANDS, PLATFORMS AND COINS', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'AN OPEN WORLD: MOVE, CLIMB AND FIGHT, FIRST OR THIRD PERSON', family: 'SHOOTER' },\n  { id: 'horror', label: 'HORROR', about: 'A MANSION BY FLASHLIGHT: FIXED CAMERAS, FEW BULLETS', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'racing', label: 'RACING', about: 'A KART CIRCUIT: DRIFTS, ITEMS, A SHORTCUT, TWO PLAYERS', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'flight', label: 'FLIGHT', about: 'ON RAILS TO THE BASE, A BOSS IN FREE FLIGHT', family: 'SHOOTER' },\n  { id: 'crawler', label: 'CRAWLER', about: 'A DUNGEON IN FIRST PERSON: A PARTY OF FOUR, A CELL AT A TIME', family: 'RPG' }\n];\n// a prompt in the player's own controls ('J Sword', 'X Sword', 'ATTACK Sword' on a touch screen)\n// (a phone or tablet before its first touch counts too: a coarse pointer and nothing else used yet)\nconst coarse = typeof matchMedia === 'function' && matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;\nconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch' || (coarse && game.input.lastDevice === 'keyboard');\n// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does\nconst pickOnStart = m => { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { game.input.consumeAll(); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\nlet active = null;               // the world of the scene that is playing (the shared keys turn its camera)\n\n/* ---- the camera: C cycles the view, the chase camera and first person; V, [ ] and 0 work on the view (and turn the\n * others) ---- */\nconst CAMS = ['view', 'chase', 'first'], CAM_NAME = { chase: 'CHASE CAMERA', first: 'FIRST PERSON' };\nconst viewName = () => game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW';\n/** the camera key (input action 'camera'), read in a slice's update */\nfunction cameraKey(world) {\n  if (!game.input.pressed('camera')) return;\n  const c = world.camera, m = CAMS[(CAMS.indexOf(c.mode) + 1) % CAMS.length]; c.set(m); game.note(m === 'view' ? viewName() : CAM_NAME[m]);\n}\naddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (e.repeat || e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey || e.altKey || game.paused) return;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyM') { A.mute(); return; }\n  if (active && ['fixed', 'zones'].includes(active.camera.mode)) return;   // (a slice that runs its own camera, or fixed cameras by room: its keys are its own)\n  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); if (active) active.camera.set('view'); game.note(viewName()); }\n  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }\n  else if (e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n});\n/** a dark veil over the 3D picture (the title's lower third, a game over) */\nconst veil = (g, r, y0, a = .55) => { g.save(); g.fillStyle = '#05030c'; g.globalAlpha = a; g.fillRect(0, y0, r.bw, r.bh - y0); g.restore(); g._c = null; };\n\n/* ---- TITLE: a little stage in 3D, the slices' heroes on it in torchlight, the camera turning round them ---- */\nconst TITLE_LEVEL = {\n  rows: [\n    '                    ',\n    ' ################## ',\n    ' #t......PP......t# ',\n    ' #.......PP.......# ',\n    ' #................# ',\n    ' #....========....# ',\n    ' #....========....# ',\n    ' #....========....# ',\n    ' #.....^^^^^^.....# ',\n    ' #t..............t# ',\n    ' #................# ',\n    '                    '],\n  legend: { '=': { floor: 8, side: 'block', color: '#4a4360' }, '^': { stairs: 'n', floor: 8 } }\n};\nlet title = null;\nconst TITLE_CAST = [\n  { x: -18, face: 0, rig: () => new E.Humanoid({ cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.5 }, colors: { cloth: '#2f8f86', cape: '#c8452f', capeIn: '#7a2622', hair: '#2e2230' } }) },\n  { x: 18, face: 0, rig: () => new E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, hat: 'cap', build: 'heroic', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0', hat: '#d83a2a' } }) }\n];\nBOOT.push(['The title stage', () => {\n  const w = new W3(game, { level: TITLE_LEVEL, fog: { near: 140, far: 600 }, torchShadows: 1 }), cx = w.width / 2, cy = 6.5 * 16;\n  const heroes = TITLE_CAST.map(c => { const a = w.hero({ x: cx + c.x, y: cy, rig: c.rig(), facing: Math.PI / 2 }); a.anim = { pose: null }; return a; });\n  const slime = w.mob({ x: cx - 44, y: cy + 30, blob: new E.Blob({ R: 6.2, face: 'front', ears: 'cat' }) }), wisp = w.mob({ x: cx + 44, y: cy + 24, orb: { color: '#c78bff' }, fly: true });\n  w.thing('star', cx, cy - 26, 8 + 12, { spin: .35, bob: 3 });\n  w.camera.set('fixed');\n  title = { world: w, cx, cy, heroes, slime, wisp, t: 0 };\n}]);\n/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\nconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\nlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\nscenes.title = {\n  view: 'iso', input: W3.INPUT,\n  enter() { A.music('title'); active = null; game.resetCamera(); },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n    const T = title, w = T.world; T.t += dt;\n    // the camera turns slowly round the stage; the heroes swing now and then; the slime hops, the wisp hovers\n    const a = T.t * .18 + 2.2, d = 120;\n    w.camera.fixed = { x: T.cx + Math.cos(a) * d, y: T.cy + Math.sin(a) * d, z: 58, yaw: a + Math.PI, pitch: -.36, fov: 50 };\n    T.heroes.forEach((h, i) => {\n      const u = (T.t * .45 + i * .5) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n      h.facing = Math.atan2(Math.sin(a), Math.cos(a)) + (i ? -.5 : .5); h.anim = { attack: swing };\n    });\n    if (T.slime.grounded && (T.t % 1.6) < dt) T.slime.vz = 140;\n    T.slime.anim = { squash: T.slime.grounded ? 0 : .2 };\n    T.wisp.vz = (8 + 20 + Math.sin(T.t * 2) * 3 - T.wisp.z) * 4;\n    w.step(dt);\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    title.world.draw(r);\n    const top = Math.max(10, Math.round(r.H * .1)), my = Math.round(r.H * .58);\n    titleMenu.y = my;\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      veil(g, r, my - 14, .5);\n      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n      E.font.title(g, '3D', r.W / 2, top + 36, { align: 'center', scale: 3, colors: ['#e8fcff', '#8af4ff', '#2aa0e0'], depth: 2, depthColor: '#14304a' });\n      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    });\n    titleMenu.draw(r);\n    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu' : 'Arrows + Enter or click   M mute';\n    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n  }\n};\n\n/* ---- GAME OVER and COURSE CLEAR: shared by every slice, over its world, frozen where it ended ---- */\nconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 'center', onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? over.from : 'title') });\nlet over = { from: 'title', world: null, won: false, lines: [] };\nscenes.over = {\n  input: W3.INPUT,\n  enter(d) { over = Object.assign({ won: false, lines: [] }, d); overMenu.i = 0; A.music(over.won ? 'victory' : null); if (!over.won) A.sfx('die'); active = null; },\n  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n  draw(r) {\n    if (over.world) over.world.draw(r);\n    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 70; overMenu.y = y + 70 + over.lines.length * 10;\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      veil(g, r, 0, .6);\n      E.font.title(g, over.won ? over.title || 'CLEAR!' : 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: over.won ? ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347'] : ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: over.won ? '#3a2008' : '#3a0810' });\n      over.lines.forEach((l, i) => E.font.text(g, l, r.W / 2, y + 44 + i * 10, '#f0e6ff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false }));\n    });\n    overMenu.draw(r);\n  }\n};\n/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 7  CRAWLER  (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder, King's Field). @modules grid\n * The Lantern Vaults in first person, a cell at a time: W and S (or up and down) step forward and back, A and D turn a\n * quarter turn, Q and E step aside, each one tweened. A party of four, their portraits under the view: two in front who\n * fight, two behind who cast. J (or a click on the view) uses what is in front (a lever, a locked gate) or has the next\n * one ready act: a blow at what stands in front, else the mage's bolt; K the mage's bolt down the corridor, H the\n * cleric's heal, 1 to 4 (or a click on a portrait) that one's own act; Tab the map (what the party has seen: E.Fog).\n * Gates that rise (one with an iron lock), a lever on a wall, plates in the floor (one raises a gate, one springs darts);\n * wisps, slimes, the dead of the vaults and the Warden at the bottom; the stair out behind it. Settings, Turns: REAL TIME\n * (each one's gauge fills on game time, E.Turns 'atb': Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder) or TURNS (the vaults wait:\n * each step, turn or blow is the party's turn, the monsters act by their speed, E.Turns 'speed': Wizardry).\n * THE 3D: the camera 'fixed' at the party's eyes, tweened per step; a level of 2 x 2 tiles a cell, braziers in niches,\n * a ceiling and the party's lantern; world.thing gates that rise, and a lever, plates and a stair drawn by the slice;\n * mobs walked cell to cell. Deep link: #crawler/warden (the Warden's hall, its gates open). CRAWLER.run(n): a scripted\n * walk's hash (the proof); CRAWLER.bot(): to the Warden and out\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst CRAWLER = (() => {\n  const C = 32, PI = Math.PI, EYE = 25, STEP_T = .28, TURN_T = .2, MOVE_T = .4;\n  // the four ways, a quarter turn apart: 0 north, 1 east, 2 south, 3 west\n  const DX = [0, 1, 0, -1], DY = [-1, 0, 1, 0], YAW = d => -PI / 2 + d * PI / 2, WAYS = ['N', 'E', 'S', 'W'];\n  /* ---- THE VAULTS: one character a cell (2 metres: 2 x 2 of the level's tiles). # wall, . floor, @ the start (facing\n   * north), n a wall with a brazier in a niche, L a wall with a lever, G a gate (raised by what is wired to it), K a gate\n   * with an iron lock, P a plate (raises a gate), T a plate that springs darts, X the stair out, i the iron key, h a\n   * flask, w wisps, s slimes, k the dead, W the Warden ---- */\n  const MAP = [\n    '#########n#n###n###n#',\n    '#######.....i.#..X..#',\n    '#######....k..#..W..#',\n    '#######.s.....#.....#',\n    '#.....#.....s.###G###',\n    'n.w.h.#.......#..P..n',\n    '#w....#.......#...k.#',\n    '###.######.######K###',\n    '###............T..###',\n    '######n###G##########',\n    '########.....########',\n    '#######L.....n#######',\n    '########..@..########',\n    '#####################'];\n  const MW = MAP[0].length, MH = MAP.length, at = (x, y) => (MAP[y] || '')[x] || '#';\n  const WALLS = '#nL', wallCell = (x, y) => WALLS.includes(at(x, y));\n  // what is wired to what: a lever's or a plate's cell -> the gate it raises\n  const WIRES = { '7,11': '10,9', '17,5': '17,4' };\n  // a wall cell's open side (a niche's brazier, a lever's face): the first way with floor beyond it\n  const openSide = (x, y) => [0, 1, 2, 3].find(d => !wallCell(x + DX[d], y + DY[d]));\n  // the level: each cell 2 x 2 tiles; a niche holds a brazier ('t') in the tile on its open side\n  const NICHE = [['t#', '##'], ['#t', '##'], ['##', 't#'], ['t#', '##']];\n  const rows = [];\n  for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let k = 0; k < 2; k++) {\n    let row = ''; for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) { const c = at(x, y); row += c === 'n' ? NICHE[openSide(x, y)][k] : wallCell(x, y) ? '##' : '..'; }\n    rows.push(row);\n  }\n  const LEVEL = { rows, ground: 'flagstone', colors: { base: '#4a4656', dark: '#34303e', light: '#5a5668' }, side: 'brick', color: '#4e4858', legend: {} };\n  const mid = c => c * C + C / 2;\n\n  /* ---- THE PARTY: two in front who fight, two behind who cast; each one's portrait is its rig's (drawPortrait) ---- */\n  const PARTY = [\n    { name: 'BRAM', role: 'FIGHTER', hp: 46, speed: 100, hit: [8, 13], rig: { build: 'heroic', hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#8a92a0' }, colors: { cloth: '#7a3a2e', pants: '#3a3440', hair: '#4a2e1e', skin: '#d8a888', metal: '#b8c0cc' } } },\n    { name: 'TESK', role: 'ROGUE', hp: 34, speed: 135, hit: [5, 10], rig: { hood: true, colors: { cloth: '#3a5a3e', pants: '#2e2a26', hair: '#2a3a2c', skin: '#c89070' } } },\n    { name: 'MAREN', role: 'CLERIC', hp: 30, mp: 16, speed: 90, heal: [12, 19], rig: { hair: 'long', hat: 'band', colors: { cloth: '#d8d0b8', pants: '#8a7a5a', hair: '#c8a050', skin: '#e8c0a0', hat: '#c8a040' } } },\n    { name: 'QUILL', role: 'MAGE', hp: 22, mp: 18, speed: 85, bolt: [11, 18], rig: { hat: 'pointed', weapon: null, colors: { cloth: '#3a3a7a', pants: '#2a2a4a', hair: '#e0e0e8', skin: '#e0b090', hat: '#3a3a7a' } } }];\n  const BOLT_MP = 4, HEAL_MP = 3;\n  /* ---- THE MONSTERS: hp, a blow's damage, speed (100: a turn as the party's), how far they see (cells) ---- */\n  const BONE = { bone: '#d8cfb4', cloth: '#2c2434', belt: '#5a4a38', metal: '#b3b8c0', metalDk: '#636872', hilt: '#6a5038' };\n  const WARDEN = { cloth: '#3a3a52', pants: '#2a2832', boot: '#1e1c24', belt: '#5a4a30', trim: '#9a8a5a', metal: '#7a8294', metalDk: '#3e4452', skin: '#8a9aa8', hair: '#1a1a22' };\n  const KINDS = {\n    wisp: { hp: 9, dmg: [2, 4], speed: 150, sight: 4, z: 16 },\n    slime: { hp: 20, dmg: [3, 6], speed: 70, sight: 3 },\n    skeleton: { hp: 28, dmg: [4, 8], speed: 100, sight: 5, move: 'slash' },\n    warden: { hp: 120, dmg: [6, 10], speed: 95, sight: 6, move: 'overhead', boss: true }\n  };\n  const MARK = { w: 'wisp', s: 'slime', k: 'skeleton', W: 'warden' };\n\n  /* ---- THINGS drawn by this slice (the engine's kinds are in its manual): a lever on a wall, a plate in the floor, the\n   * stair out (an arch over steps down, lit once the Warden falls) ---- */\n  W3.THINGS.wallLever = (p, t) => {   // its local +y points out of the wall\n    const a = t.on ? -1 : 1;\n    p.box(0, .8, 20, 6, 1.6, 9, '#4a4452').box(0, 1.8, 20, 2, .8, 5.5, '#24202a')\n      .tube(0, 2.2, 20, 0, 3.6, 20 + a * 5, .55, '#a8a8b8').ball(0, 3.8, 20 + a * 5.4, 1.1, 1.1, 1.1, t.on ? '#4ae070' : '#e8483a');\n  };\n  W3.THINGS.plate = (p, t) => { const s = t.on ? .2 : 1, c = t.color || '#6a6474'; p.box(0, 0, s / 2, 22, 22, s, c).box(0, 0, s + .05, 17, 17, .1, E.shade(c, -.2)); };\n  W3.THINGS.stair = (p, t) => {\n    const s = '#5a5468';\n    p.box(-13, 0, 19, 4, 5, 38, s).box(13, 0, 19, 4, 5, 38, s).box(0, 0, 39, 30, 6, 4, s);\n    for (let k = 0; k < 4; k++) p.box(0, -2 - k * 3, -1 - k * 2.5, 22, 3, 2, '#3a3644');   // the steps going down\n    if (t.on) p.glow(0, 0, 16, 5 + Math.sin((t.t || 0) * 3) * .8, '#9ae8ff').halo(0, 0, 16, 18, [.15, .3, .38]);\n    else p.box(0, 0, 18, 22, 1, 34, '#14121a');\n  };\n\n  /* ---- SOUNDS AND MUSIC (the step sequencer's format: original songs) ---- */\n  const SOUNDS = {\n    step: { wave: 'noise', freq: 320, to: 120, dur: .07, vol: .1, filter: 'lowpass' }, turn: { wave: 'noise', freq: 900, to: 500, dur: .06, vol: .05 },\n    thud: [{ wave: 'square', freq: 90, to: 50, dur: .1, vol: .2 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 300, dur: .06, vol: .12 }],\n    swing: { wave: 'noise', freq: 2600, to: 800, dur: .1, vol: .12 }, bolt: [{ wave: 'saw', freq: 220, to: 880, dur: .18, vol: .16 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 3000, to: 600, dur: .2, vol: .1 }],\n    lever: [{ wave: 'square', freq: 260, to: 140, dur: .08, vol: .2 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 1200, dur: .05, vol: .12, delay: .09 }],\n    gate: { wave: 'saw', freq: 70, to: 110, dur: .9, vol: .12, vib: [12, .1], filter: 'lowpass' }, plate: { wave: 'square', freq: 140, to: 90, dur: .1, vol: .2 },\n    dart: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 4000, to: 2000, dur: .05, vol: .2 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 4000, to: 2000, dur: .05, vol: .2, delay: .07 }],\n    locked: { wave: 'square', freq: 180, dur: .05, vol: .16 }, unlock: { wave: 'square', freq: 660, arp: [0, 7], step: .06, dur: .14, vol: .18 },\n    rattle: { wave: 'noise', freq: 2200, arp: [0, 3, 0, 5], step: .04, dur: .2, vol: .1 }, squelch: { wave: 'sine', freq: 140, to: 60, dur: .16, vol: .25 },\n    zap: { wave: 'square', freq: 1400, to: 300, dur: .1, vol: .1 }, roar: [{ wave: 'saw', freq: 110, to: 55, dur: 1, vol: .2, vib: [7, .12] }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 500, to: 120, dur: .8, vol: .15, filter: 'lowpass' }]\n  };\n  const VAULT = { bpm: 72, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the vaults: a slow figure over a drone, water dripping\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .26, notes: 'A1 - - - - - - - | A1 - - - - - - - | F1 - - - - - - - | E1 - - - - - - -' },\n    { wave: 'pulse25', vol: .05, notes: 'A3 . C4 . E4 . . . | D4 . C4 . B3 . . . | A3 . C4 . F4 . E4 . | E4 . . . G#3 . . .' },\n    { wave: 'sine', vol: .07, notes: '. . . . . . E5 . | . . . . . . . . | . . . . . . . A5 | . . . . . . . .' }] };\n  const FIGHT = { bpm: 128, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the Warden\n    { wave: 'saw', vol: .06, notes: 'A3 A3 . A3 C4 . A3 . | G3 G3 . G3 Bb3 . G3 . | F3 F3 . F3 A3 . F3 . | E3 . G#3 . B3 . E4 .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'A1 . A1 . A1 . A1 . | G1 . G1 . G1 . G1 . | F1 . F1 . F1 . F1 . | E1 . E1 . E1 . E1 .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . h k s . h . | k k h . s . h h' }] };\n\n  /* ---- THE STATE ---- */\n  let world = null, hero = null, lamp = null, grid = null, fog = null, turns = null, rnd = Math.random, mode = 'real', scripted = false;\n  let party = null, S = null, foes = [], gates = {}, levers = [], plates = {}, items = [], stair = null, bolts = [], keys = null;\n  let total = 0, msg = null, showMap = false, song = null, ended = 0, slashT = 0, phase = 'party', took = 0, rounds = 0;\n  BOOT.push(['The vaults', () => {\n    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(SOUNDS)) A.define(k, v);\n    world = new W3(game, { level: LEVEL, torchLights: 4, torchShadows: 0, torchPower: 16, torchReach: 160, torchColor: '#ffb070', lights: 2,\n      ambient: ['#5a5478', '#221e2a', 3.4], fog: { color: '#050407', near: 40, far: 250 }, sky: '#050407', camera: { mode: 'fixed' },\n      onDraw: w => {   // the ceiling over the vaults, the bolts in flight, the wisps' zaps\n        w.pen.at().box(w.width / 2, w.depth / 2, 50, w.width, w.depth, 4, '#1c1a22');   // (at(): the pen's origin back at the world's)\n        for (const b of bolts) w.glow(b.x, b.y, b.z, 3.2, '#ffb14a', { light: true });\n        for (const e of foes) if (e.zap > 0) w.pen.at().bar(e.x, e.y, e.z + 2, S.x, S.y, EYE - 6, .6, .6, '#bff4ff');\n      } });\n  }]);\n\n  /** a fresh descent (seed: the dice; m: 'real' or 'turns', else the player's setting) */\n  function reset(seed = 1, m = null) {\n    world.reset(); rnd = E.rng(seed); mode = m || game.settings.crawlTurns || 'real';\n    const st = MAP.findIndex(r => r.includes('@')), sx = MAP[st].indexOf('@');\n    hero = world.hero({ x: mid(sx), y: mid(st), r: 4, visible: false }); world.camera.follow(hero);\n    S = { cx: sx, cy: st, dir: 0, x: mid(sx), y: mid(st), yaw: YAW(0), px: mid(sx), py: mid(st), pyaw: YAW(0), from: null, t: 0, dur: 0, bump: 0, act: 0 };\n    party = PARTY.map((o, i) => ({ i, name: o.name, role: o.role, front: i < 2, max: o.hp, hp: o.hp, mpMax: o.mp || 0, mp: o.mp || 0, speed: o.speed, o, hurtT: 0, flash: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid(Object.assign({ speedRef: 60 }, o.rig)), _turn: 100 }));\n    if (!lamp) lamp = world.light({ color: '#ffd8a0', reach: 190, power: 10 });\n    keys = new Set(); items = []; bolts = []; foes = []; gates = {}; levers = []; plates = {}; stair = null;\n    for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) {\n      const c = at(x, y), k = x + ',' + y;\n      if (c === 'G' || c === 'K') {   // a gate across its corridor (walls east and west: it spans x)\n        const ns = wallCell(x - 1, y) && wallCell(x + 1, y);\n        gates[k] = { cx: x, cy: y, up: false, t: world.thing('door', mid(x), mid(y), 0, { yaw: ns ? 0 : PI / 2, w: 32, h: 46, color: '#26242c', frame: '#3a3444', locked: c === 'K' ? 'iron' : null, solid: true }) };\n      } else if (c === 'L') {\n        const d = openSide(x, y), fx = x + DX[d], fy = y + DY[d];   // its face: toward the floor cell beside it\n        levers.push({ cx: fx, cy: fy, dir: (d + 2) % 4, gate: WIRES[k], t: world.thing('wallLever', mid(x) + DX[d] * C / 2, mid(y) + DY[d] * C / 2, 0, { yaw: Math.atan2(DY[d], DX[d]) - PI / 2 }) });\n      } else if (c === 'P' || c === 'T') plates[k] = { trap: c === 'T', gate: WIRES[k], t: world.thing('plate', mid(x), mid(y), 0, { color: c === 'T' ? '#625c6a' : '#6e6878' }) };\n      else if (c === 'X') stair = { cx: x, cy: y, t: world.thing('stair', mid(x), mid(y) - 6, 0, { on: false }) };\n      else if (c === 'i') items.push({ cx: x, cy: y, kind: 'key', t: world.thing('key', mid(x), mid(y), 5, { color: '#8a8c98', spin: .3, bob: 1.5 }) });\n      else if (c === 'h') items.push({ cx: x, cy: y, kind: 'flask', t: world.thing('potion', mid(x), mid(y), 0, { color: '#e04a4a', spin: .2 }) });\n      else if (MARK[c]) foes.push(spawn(MARK[c], x, y));\n    }\n    total = foes.length;\n    grid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => open(x, y), opaque: (x, y) => wallCell(x, y) || !!(gates[x + ',' + y] && gates[x + ',' + y].t.open < .5) });\n    fog = new E.Fog(grid); look();\n    makeTurns(); msg = null; showMap = false; song = null; ended = 0; slashT = 0; phase = 'party'; took = 0; rounds = 0;\n    world.camera.set('fixed'); place(0);\n  }\n  function spawn(type, x, y) {\n    const k = KINDS[type], X = mid(x), Y = mid(y);\n    const e = type === 'wisp' ? world.mob({ x: X, y: Y, z: k.z, r: 4, half: 0, fly: true, orb: { color: '#8ae0ff', r: 3.6 } })\n      : type === 'slime' ? world.mob({ x: X, y: Y, r: 6, half: 0, mass: 2, blob: new E.Blob({ R: 7, face: 'front', colors: { base: '#5ac86a', dk: '#2e7a3e', lt: '#a8f0a0' } }) })\n      : world.mob({ x: X, y: Y, r: type === 'warden' ? 8 : 4.5, half: type === 'warden' ? 12 : 8, mass: type === 'warden' ? 8 : 1.4,\n        rig: type === 'warden' ? new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.45, build: 'bulky', armor: true, sleeves: 'long', bladeLen: 13, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#5a5e6e' }, eyeGlow: '#7ad8ff', colors: WARDEN, speedRef: 45 })\n          : new E.Humanoid({ build: 'skeleton', bladeLen: 9, colors: BONE, speedRef: 40 }) });\n    return Object.assign(e, { type, k, cx: x, cy: y, hp: k.hp, max: k.hp, speed: k.speed, awake: false, atk: null, hitT: 0, zap: 0, tx: X, ty: Y, deadT: 0, blows: 0, _turn: 0, facing: PI / 2 });\n  }\n  /** the turns: real time, each one's gauge on game time ('atb'); turns, the party one actor among the monsters ('speed') */\n  function makeTurns() {\n    const live = foes.filter(e => e.hp > 0);\n    turns = mode === 'turns' ? new E.Turns([S, ...live], { mode: 'speed' }) : new E.Turns([...party.filter(m => m.hp > 0), ...live], { mode: 'atb', fill: .55 });\n    S.speed = 100; for (const m of party) m._turn = mode === 'turns' ? 100 : Math.min(m._turn, 100);\n  }\n  const say = (text, t = 2.4) => { msg = { text, t }; };\n  const gateAt = (x, y) => gates[x + ',' + y];\n  const foeAt = (x, y) => foes.find(e => e.hp > 0 && e.cx === x && e.cy === y);\n  /** can a body stand in this cell (a wall, a gate down: no) */\n  function open(x, y) { if (wallCell(x, y)) return false; const g = gateAt(x, y); return !g || (g.up && g.t.open > .85); }\n  const alive = () => party.filter(m => m.hp > 0);\n  /** the party sees: the fog's field of view, and the monsters it falls on wake */\n  function look() {\n    fog.update([{ cx: S.cx, cy: S.cy, r: 5 }]);\n    for (const e of foes) if (e.hp > 0 && !e.awake && fog.visible([e.cx, e.cy]) && Math.abs(e.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(e.cy - S.cy) <= e.k.sight) wake(e);\n  }\n  function wake(e) { e.awake = true; A.sfx(e.type === 'slime' ? 'squelch' : e.type === 'wisp' ? 'zap' : e.type === 'warden' ? 'roar' : 'rattle'); if (e.type === 'warden') say('THE WARDEN WAKES', 3); }\n\n  /* ---- MOVING: a step or a turn, tweened; bumping a wall ---- */\n  function place(u) {   // where the eyes are this step (u: the tween's 0..1)\n    const s = u * u * (3 - 2 * u), F = S.from;\n    S.px = S.x; S.py = S.y; S.pyaw = S.yaw;\n    if (F) { S.x = lerp(F[0], mid(S.cx), s); S.y = lerp(F[1], mid(S.cy), s); S.yaw = F[2] + E.angDiff(F[2], YAW(S.dir)) * s; }\n    else { S.x = mid(S.cx); S.y = mid(S.cy); S.yaw = YAW(S.dir); }\n    const b = Math.sin(Math.min(1, S.bump) * PI) * 4;   // a bump into a wall: a lurch forward and back\n    hero.place(S.x + Math.cos(S.yaw) * b, S.y + Math.sin(S.yaw) * b, 0);\n    world.camera.fixed = { x: S.x + Math.cos(S.yaw) * (b - 4), y: S.y + Math.sin(S.yaw) * (b - 4), z: EYE + Math.sin(s * PI) * (F && F[3] ? .8 : 0), yaw: S.yaw, pitch: -.04, fov: 74 };\n  }\n  const busy = () => S.dur > 0 && S.t < S.dur;\n  /** try to step one cell along way d (relative to nothing: 0..3 on the map); true when the party moves */\n  function stepTo(d) {\n    const x = S.cx + DX[d], y = S.cy + DY[d];\n    if (!open(x, y) || foeAt(x, y)) { S.bump = .001; A.sfx('thud'); const g = gateAt(x, y); if (g && !g.up && !scripted) say(g.t.locked ? 'A GATE WITH AN IRON LOCK' : 'THE GATE WILL NOT BUDGE'); return false; }\n    S.from = [S.x, S.y, S.yaw, 1]; S.cx = x; S.cy = y; S.t = 0; S.dur = STEP_T; A.sfx('step'); return true;\n  }\n  function turnBy(s) { S.from = [S.x, S.y, S.yaw, 0]; S.dir = (S.dir + s + 4) % 4; S.t = 0; S.dur = TURN_T; A.sfx('turn'); return true; }\n  /** the party has come into its cell: plates, things to take, the stair */\n  function arrive() {\n    look(); const k = S.cx + ',' + S.cy, pl = plates[k];\n    if (pl && !pl.t.on) {\n      pl.t.on = true; A.sfx('plate');\n      if (pl.trap) { A.sfx('dart'); say('DARTS FROM THE WALLS!'); for (const m of alive().filter(m => m.front)) hurtMember(m, 4 + ((rnd() * 4) | 0)); }\n      else { raise(gates[pl.gate]); say('A GRINDING, FAR OFF', 2.6); }\n    }\n    for (const it of items.slice()) if (it.cx === S.cx && it.cy === S.cy) {\n      world.remove(it.t); items.splice(items.indexOf(it), 1); took++; A.sfx('pickup');\n      if (it.kind === 'key') { keys.add('iron'); say('THE IRON KEY'); } else { for (const m of alive()) heal(m, 15); say('A FLASK: EVERYONE FEELS BETTER'); }\n    }\n    if (stair && S.cx === stair.cx && S.cy === stair.cy) { if (stair.t.on) win(); else if (!scripted) say('THE STAIR IS SEALED: SOMETHING HOLDS IT'); }\n  }\n  function raise(g) { if (!g || g.up) return; g.up = true; g.t.locked = null; A.sfx('gate'); }\n  /** J at what is in front: a lever on this wall, a locked gate; true when it used something */\n  function use() {\n    const fx = S.cx + DX[S.dir], fy = S.cy + DY[S.dir];\n    const lv = levers.find(l => l.cx === S.cx && l.cy === S.cy && l.dir === S.dir);\n    if (lv) { lv.t.on = !lv.t.on; A.sfx('lever'); if (lv.t.on) { raise(gates[lv.gate]); say('A LEVER: SOMEWHERE A GATE RISES'); } return true; }\n    const g = gateAt(fx, fy);\n    if (g && !g.up && g.t.locked) {\n      const r = world.unlock(g.t, { has: k => keys.has(k), remove: k => keys.delete(k) });\n      if (r === 'unlocked') { A.sfx('unlock'); raise(g); say('THE IRON KEY TURNS'); } else { A.sfx('locked'); say('LOCKED: IT WANTS AN IRON KEY'); }\n      return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  /* ---- FIGHTING: the front rank's blows at what stands in front, the mage's bolt, the cleric's heal ---- */\n  const roll = ([a, b]) => a + ((rnd() * (b - a + 1)) | 0);\n  const ahead = () => foeAt(S.cx + DX[S.dir], S.cy + DY[S.dir]);\n  /** member m acts by i","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-build--20261103-202613--x53986f-work/6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a/tool-results/bth090424.txt","persistedOutputSize":54183},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014U3hsAsGpjfutDyVbmeHBR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
