{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghBArtn86mLL7Z5WSspE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VtsmnPRyYckzDYpNqorfTf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202613__x53986f/work/EyeOf*/ && wc -c _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/*.md && cut -c1-600 _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md | head -150"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6003,"cache_read_input_tokens":125004,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6003},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"7ec54497-30db-482c-9777-931ba359bc58","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:27:03.547Z","request_id":"req_011CghBArZgc14g9tRb8fBM2","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VtsmnPRyYckzDYpNqorfTf":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202613__x53986f/work/EyeOf*/ && wc -c _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/*.md && cut -c1-600 _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md | head -150"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VtsmnPRyYckzDYpNqorfTf","type":"tool_result","content":"114712 _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md\n192446 _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md\n 67603 _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/API.md\n  6295 _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/README.md\n381056 total\n# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `[dx, dy]`) |\n| Screen positions | pixels of the game's own low-resolution buffer (`game.screen.W` × `H`) |\n| Colors | `'#rrggbb'` strings |\n\n- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n\n## Examples\n\nEach runs in `tools/contract-test.mjs`.\n\n```js headless\n// a game with no display, in Node or a test: fixed steps, scripted input, its state\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\nconst hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\ngame.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\ngame.advance(0.25);   // 30 fixed steps of 1/120 s, at once\nif (!(hero.x > 55 && hero.z > 20)) throw new Error('the hero should run right and be in the air');\ngame.dispose();\n```\n\n```js heights\n// a guard on a roof, a hero in the street: sight, reach and a climb read heights the same way\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\nconst guard = { x: 56, y: 40, z: 40, facing: Math.PI }, hero = { x: 36, y: 40, z: 0, r: 5 };\nif (!map.sight(guard, hero)) throw new Error('eyes on a roof see down into the street');\nif (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\nconst up = map.ledge(hero, 0);   // east, toward the roof\nif (!up || up.z !== 40) throw new Error('a ledge to climb onto the roof');\n```\n\n## Contents\n\nThe line each section starts on, and the name its classes' instances go by: `E.Attack: slash` lists its members as `slash.start`.\n\n- 108 The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n- 119 Math\n- 194 Pixel primitives\n- 213 Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n- 246 Screen; game.screen\n- 268 Input; E.Input: input\n- 353 Pixel font\n- 364 Lighting; game.lights\n- 383 Particles; E.Particles: game.particles\n- 403 Renderer; r\n- 451 Game; E.Game: game\n- 562 Standard features; settings, fullscreen\n- 579 10c. Boot\n- 584 10d. Tweens and scripts; E.Script: script, E.Tween: tween\n- 601 10e. Paths; E.Path: path\n- 611 10g. Weather\n- 615 10k. Save slots; E.Saves: saves\n- 638 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\n- 711 Blob rig; E.Blob: blob\n- 731 Tile map; E.TileMap: map\n- 794 Materials\n- 815 Flow field; E.FlowField: flow\n- 833 Texture helpers for floortex functions\n- 844 Platform map; E.PlatformMap: level\n- 878 Platformer; E.Platformer: hero\n- 919 Body; E.Body: body\n- 939 Actions; E.Action: action\n- 961 17c. Mover; E.Mover: mover\n- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n- 1017 Bullets; E.Bullets: shots\n- 1037 Spatial hash; E.SpatialHash: grid\n- 1047 Audio; game.audio\n- 1079 Backdrops; E.Backdrop: backdrop\n- 1087 21c. Props\n- 1092 21e. Shapes\n- 1104 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\n- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n- 1190 Gpu lighting (webgpu); game.gpu\n- 1211 Sessions\n- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n- 1255 Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js); E.Click: click, E.Walkbox: walkbox\n- 1300 Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js); E.Car: car, E.Race: race\n- 1338 Module fight: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training (engine/modules/fight.js); E.FightAI: fightai, E.FightSelect: fightselect, E.FightStage: fightstage, E.Fighter: fighter, E.Match: match\n- 1419 Module gen: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed (engine/modules/gen.js)\n- 1430 Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js); E.Fog: fog, E.Grid: grid, E.GridMover: gridmover, E.Turns: turns\n- 1489 Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js); E.Mode7: mode7\n- 1512 Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js); E.Physics: physics\n- 1541 Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js); E.Rhythm: rhythm\n- 1573 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n- 1590 Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js); E.World: world\n- 1619 Module rpg: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters (engine/modules/rpg.js); E.RPG: rpg\n- 1638 Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engine/modules/songs.js)\n- 1646 Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/modules/story.js); E.Story: story\n- 1675 Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js); E.Clock: clock, E.Strategy: strategy\n- 1721 Module terrain: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks (engine/modules/terrain.js); E.Terrain: terrain\n\n## The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n\n- `E.DEG: 0.017453292519943295`: π/180, one degree in radians (angle * DEG)\n- `E.TAU: 6.283185307179586`: 2π, a full turn in radians\n- `E.build: \"dev-build\"`: the commit this copy was built from, a placeholder in the repo that tools/stamp.mjs replaces when the site deploys (e.g. 'a1b2c3d 2026-10-07')\n- `E.current: null`: the latest game made (My3D2dge.current, for tools and tests)\n- `E.name: \"my-3D2dge\"`: the engine's name, 'my-3D2dge'\n- `E.version: \"0.85.2\"`: the release (package.json, written everywhere by node tools/version.mjs)\n- `E.versionLabel()`: 'v0.7.0 · a1b2c3d 2026-10-07': the label to show on screens and in reports\n- `E.warn(key, msg)`: one console warning per distinct problem, prefixed so tools (and people) can spot engine advice: warn(key, message)\n\n## 1. Math\n\n- `E.HEIGHTS: eye, chest, level, step`: the numbers of THE HEIGHT RULES, which collision, standing, sight, reach, navigation and drawing all read (API.md, \"Heights\", and the API index's head give the rules), in world units above a body's feet. The defaults fit a size-1.3 Humanoid; a body's own eye and chest override these (crouching lowers them)\n- `E.V3`: small 3D vector helpers on [x, y, z] arrays\n- `E.V3.add(a, b)`: a + b\n- `E.V3.dot(a, b)`: dot product\n- `E.V3.len(a)`: length\n- `E.V3.lerp(a, b, t)`: the point t of the way from a to b\n- `E.V3.mul(a, s)`: a scaled by s\n- `E.V3.norm(a)`: unit vector the same way\n- `E.V3.rz(v, a)`: v turned by angle a (radians) about the z axis\n- `E.V3.sub(a, b)`: a - b\n- `E.angDiff(a, b)`: the shortest signed turn from angle a to angle b, -π..π (radians)\n- `E.angleTo(a, b)`: ground angle from a to b (radians, 0 = east, PI/2 = south)\n- `E.approach(a, b, s)`: a moved toward b by at most s, never past it: approach(speed, top, accel * dt)\n- `E.approachAng(a, b, s)`: angle a turned toward b by at most s radians: facing = approachAng(facing, target, turnSpeed * dt)\n- `E.arc(a, b, g, o = {})` †: the throw from a to b ({ x, y, z }) under gravity g (units a second squared, pulling z down): a lob to a teammate's feet, a grenade, a leap to a ledge. o: { apex: how far it rises over the higher end (24), or time: the seconds it flies, or speed: a launch speed (the lower arc that reaches; null when it can't) } -> { vx, vy, vz, t }\n- `E.bayer(x, y)` †: the 4 x 4 ordered-dither threshold 0..1 at pixel (x, y): pixel on when value > bayer(x, y)\n- `E.chance(p)`: true with probability p (0..1)\n- `E.clamp(v, a, b)`: v kept between a and b\n- `E.ctx2d(c)`: a canvas's 2D context with smoothing off (crisp pixels)\n- `E.dist(a, b)`: distance between two objects with x, y (and optional z)\n- `E.ease`: easing curves for u 0..1: linear, outQuad, inQuad, inOut (inOutQuad), outCubic, outBack (it overshoots a little more than Penner's: 1.9), and the rest of Penner's set (sine, quad, cubic, back, elastic and bounce, each in, out and inOut: inSine, outSine, inOutSine, ...), the names every tween library uses (section 1b)\n- `E.ease.inBack(u)` †: pulls back before it goes\n- `E.ease.inBounce(u)` †: bounces, then leaps away\n- `E.ease.inCubic(u)` †: slower start than inQuad\n- `E.ease.inElastic(u)` †: wobbles, then springs away\n- `E.ease.inOut(u)`: slow start and end\n- `E.ease.inOutBack(u)` †: pulls back, then overshoots\n- `E.ease.inOutBounce(u)` †: bounces at both ends\n- `E.ease.inOutCubic(u)` †: slow start and end, quicker between\n- `E.ease.inOutElastic(u)` †: wobbles at both ends","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"746d6d1d-0bc0-4516-b9f9-bbc5aa4a66d8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:27:03.586Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"114712 _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md\n192446 _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md\n 67603 _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/API.md\n  6295 _ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/README.md\n381056 total\n# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public na