{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghBBUzBCeRHNDqxhyUWh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015jPhXRMQR2h9kQCAcVwZTV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202613__x53986f/work/EyeOf*/ && I=_ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md; sed -n 1047,1079p $I | cut -c1-520; sed -n 1104,1160p $I | cut -c1-420; sed -n 353,364p $I | cut -c1-300; sed -n 562,579p $I | cut -c1-200 | head -5; grep -n \"menu: {\" $I | head; grep -n \"items:\" $I | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10002,"cache_read_input_tokens":141864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10002},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"91f27264-2753-400e-a4b5-935cba2ff269","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:27:13.971Z","request_id":"req_011CghBBUioxvqYSLFWcWzrA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015jPhXRMQR2h9kQCAcVwZTV":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202613__x53986f/work/EyeOf*/ && I=_ref/engine-src/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md; sed -n 1047,1079p $I | cut -c1-520; sed -n 1104,1160p $I | cut -c1-420; sed -n 353,364p $I | cut -c1-300; sed -n 562,579p $I | cut -c1-200 | head -5; grep -n \"menu: {\" $I | head; grep -n \"items:\" $I | head"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015jPhXRMQR2h9kQCAcVwZTV","type":"tool_result","content":"## 20. Audio\n\n- `E.note(n)`: note name -> frequency: E.note('A4') = 440, E.note('C#5'), E.note('Bb2'). Numbers pass through\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. stop() puts the music back\n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines). steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (l\n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## 21b. Backdrops\n## 21. Ui\n\n- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it shows: radio chatter), place: 'top' | 'middle\n- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n- `talk.game`: its game\n- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n- `menu.game`: its game\n- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels\n- `E.ui`: pixel-drawn interface pieces for r.overlay\n- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0463c')\n- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n\n## 6. Pixel font\n\n- `E.font`: Pixel fonts. 'normal' (default) is a 5x7 proportional font with lower case; 'tiny' is the 3x5 upper-case font. text(g, str, x, y, color, opts) where opts is an outline color, false, or { font: 'normal' | 'tiny', outline: '#0b0814' | false, shadow: '#000' (1 px drop shadow), gradient: ['#\n- `E.font.default` †: the font used when none is named: 'normal' (5 x 7) or 'tiny' (3 x 5)\n- `E.font.height(lines = 1, o, lineGap)`: the height in pixels of that many lines (with o's scale and font, and lineGap between them)\n- `E.font.lineHeight(o)`: pixels from one line to the next\n- `E.font.text(g, s, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o = '#0b0814')`: draw text at (x, y) (its top-left; align: 'center' or 'right' moves it) in color. o: an outline color, or { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font }; returns { w, h }\n- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align\n- `E.font.width(s, o)`: width in pixels of the widest line. opts: a scale number or { font, scale }\n- `E.font.wrap(s, maxW, o)`: split text into lines no wider than maxW pixels\n\n## 7. Lighting\n## 10b. Standard features\n\n- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its \n- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n441:- `r.game`: its game; items: this frame's queue (sorted by depth when the frame ends)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"e963f6f4-5d04-498a-9a30-1700f45e2c0f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:27:14.036Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## 20. Audio\n\n- `E.note(n)`: note name -> frequency: E.note('A4') = 440, E.note('C#5'), E.note('Bb2'). Numbers pass through\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. stop() puts the music back\n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines). steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (l\n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## 21b. Backdrops\n## 21. Ui\n\n- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it shows: radio chatter), place: 'top' | 'middle\n- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n- `talk.game`: its game\n- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n- `menu.game`: its game\n- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels\n- `E.ui`: pixel-drawn interface pieces for r.overlay\n- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0463c')\n- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n\n## 6. Pixel font\n\n- `E.font`: Pixel fonts. 'normal' (default) is a 5x7 proportional font with lower case; 'tiny' is the 3x5 upper-case font. text(g, str, x, y, color, opts) where opts is an outline color, false, or { font: 'normal' | 'tiny', outline: '#0b0814' | false, shadow: '#000' (1 px drop shadow), gradient: ['#\n- `E.font.default` †: the font used when none is named: 'normal' (5 x 7) or 'tiny' (3 x 5)\n- `E.font.height(lines = 1, o, lineGap)`: the height in pixels of that many lines (with o's scale and font, and lineGap between them)\n- `E.font.lineHeight(o)`: pixels from one line to the next\n- `E.font.text(g, s, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o = '#0b0814')`: draw text at (x, y) (its top-left; align: 'center' or 'right' moves it) in color. o: an outline color, or { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font }; returns { w, h }\n- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align\n- `E.font.width(s, o)`: width in pixels of the widest line. opts: a scale number or { font, scale }\n- `E.font.wrap(s, maxW, o)`: split text into lines no wider than maxW pixels\n\n## 7. Lighting\n## 10b. Standard features\n\n- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its \n- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n441:- `r.game`: its game; items: this frame's queue (sorted by depth when the frame ends)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015jPhXRMQR2h9kQCAcVwZTV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
