{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PzanGqGtbdjuhTY2RsekhL","type":"tool_result","content":"131:- Adjust: `new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }, { key: 'difficulty', options: ['Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard'], value: 'Normal' }], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: false }, quit: 'title' } })`, then read `game.settings.hints`. Leave parts out: `menu: false` (your own pause), `fullscreen: 'button' | false`, `corner: false`, `backGesture: false`, `autoPause: false`. `game.cornerArea()`: where the corner's buttons cover the scree\n132:- Save slots (`game.saves`): three slots and an autosave, each with its place, level and time played. `game.saves.write = () => ({ data, place, level })` and `read = save => {...}`; then `save(slot)` (0, 1, 2 or `'auto'`), `load(slot)`, `copy(a, b)`, `erase(slot)`, `autosave()`, `list()`, `latest()` (a title's Continue). `menu: { saves: true }` (or `{ slots, version, migrate(data, from) }`) puts Save (while `saves.canSave`: a save point) and Load in the pause menu, and `saves.show('save' | '\n302:  get(key, fallback = null) { try { const v = localStorage.getItem('my3d2dge:' + key); return v === null ? fallback : JSON.parse(v); } catch (e) { return fallback; } },   // the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n663:    const v = Array.isArray(r) ? r : E.RES[String(r).toLowerCase()];\n725:        const v = g.createRadialGradient(w / 2, h / 2, Math.min(w, h) * .35, w / 2, h / 2, Math.hypot(w, h) / 2); v.addColorStop(0, 'rgba(0,0,0,0)'); v.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(0,0,0,.45)'); g.fillStyle = v; g.fillRect(0, 0, c.width, c.height);\n1538:        const v = I[k];\n1551:      const v = I[k];\n1749:  w(x, y, z = 0) { const v = this.game.view; return [v.ax * x + v.ay * y - this.ix, v.bx * x + v.by * y + v.bz * z - this.iy]; }\n1837:      const v = this.view, R = Math.round(rad * 2) / 2, A = Math.round(alpha * 20) / 20, st2 = E.style.trans;\n1970:    const v = this.view, span = Math.max(1, Math.min(50, 85 - z));\n2913:    const v = this.view, k = this.zoom / (this._zoomTo || this.zoom);\n3055:  default(key) { const s = this._specs[key]; if (!s) return undefined; const v = typeof s.value === 'function' ? s.value(this._g) : s.value; return v === undefined && s.type === 'toggle' ? false : v; }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"90829edc-064e-440e-a544-079db178024d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:27:17.406Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"131:- Adjust: `new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }, { key: 'difficulty', options: ['Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard'], value: 'Normal' }], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: false }, quit: 'title' } })`, then read `game.settings.hints`. Leave parts out: `menu: false` (your own pause), `fullscreen: 'button' | false`, `corner: false`, `backGesture: false`, `autoPause: false`. `game.cornerArea()`: where the corner's buttons cover the scree\n132:- Save slots (`game.saves`): three slots and an autosave, each with its place, level and time played. `game.saves.write = () => ({ data, place, level })` and `read = save => {...}`; then `save(slot)` (0, 1, 2 or `'auto'`), `load(slot)`, `copy(a, b)`, `erase(slot)`, `autosave()`, `list()`, `latest()` (a title's Continue). `menu: { saves: true }` (or `{ slots, version, migrate(data, from) }`) puts Save (while `saves.canSave`: a save point) and Load in the pause menu, and `saves.show('save' | '\n302:  get(key, fallback = null) { try { const v = localStorage.getItem('my3d2dge:' + key); return v === null ? fallback : JSON.parse(v); } catch (e) { return fallback; } },   // the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n663:    const v = Array.isArray(r) ? r : E.RES[String(r).toLowerCase()];\n725:        const v = g.createRadialGradient(w / 2, h / 2, Math.min(w, h) * .35, w / 2, h / 2, Math.hypot(w, h) / 2); v.addColorSt