{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghFg5TqwsLtYgLr42qEA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0121qV44jq9DonnVWZ5qEnQL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-202613__x53986f/work/EyeOf*/ && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/60-input-ui.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"  for (const k of ['up', 'down', 'left', 'right', 'start', 'pause', 'confirm', 'cancel']) o[k] = D[k].slice();\",\"  for (const k of ['up', 'down', 'left', 'right', 'start', 'pause', 'confirm', 'cancel']) o[k] = D[k].slice();\\n  o.cancel = ['Backspace', ...o.cancel.filter(c => c !== 'Backspace')];\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/90-main.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"window.__game = { game, B, UI };\",\"window.__game = { game, B, UI };\\n// the hub's rule: while Create (Pad8) is held, Options (Pad9) belongs to the hub's corner bar, not to the game's pause menu\\n{ const op = game.pause.bind(game); game.pause = (r) => { if (B.inSessionEarly && game.input.held && game.input.held.has('Pad8')) return false; return op(r); }; }\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Eye of the Bolt-Holder\n\nA real-time, first-person party dungeon crawler on the my-3D2dge engine (v0.85.2), inspired by *Eye of the Beholder* (1991). One HTML file; three.js and Rapier load from jsDelivr. Everything (art, music, sound, voices) is drawn or synthesized by code.\n\n## Build, test, play\n- `node tools/build.mjs` bundles `src/*.js` (name order) with `engine/`, `hub/session.js` and the import map into `../EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-<model>-<stamp>.html`.\n- `node tools/exit.mjs` writes `../exit-interview.json` from `src/98-about.js` (the About screen's source).\n- `node tests/run.mjs [lint|sim|playthrough|browser|harness ...] [--fast]` prints only failures and one summary line.\n  - `lint` / `sim`: content lint and 110+ checks of the deterministic sim in Node (`vm`, no engine).\n  - `playthrough`: a bot plays New Game to the ending on Normal with no cheats (two seeds) and writes `tests/out/balance.txt`.\n  - `browser`: Playwright, Chromium on WebGL 2 from `file://`: boot, attract mode (10 s idle, any input exits), Quick Start, keys, Party screen, glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox / keyboard), save and load, Dev Mode, Rat Run, touch-only notice. It drives time with `game.advance()` because the software renderer runs at about 4 fps.\n  - `harness`: the AI Hub harness at `players=2`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5` and `scenario=host-leave`.\n- `tests/shoot.mjs name ...` takes screenshots into `shots/` (not part of pass or fail).\n\n## Controls\nPad (PlayStation glyphs, Xbox in Settings): left stick or d-pad up/down step, left stick left/right sidestep, d-pad left/right or right stick turn, ✕ use (hold: put down), ○ throw, □ Party Strike, △ Party, L1/R1 member, L2/R2 off/main hand, L3 camp, R3 examine, Create map, Options pause.\nKeyboard: W/S step, A/D sidestep, Q/E turn, F use, H put down, G throw, Space strike, I party, C camp, M map, J journal, X examine, 1-6 hands (Shift: off hand), Tab member. Mouse: hover to focus, click things in the view and menu items, right click strikes, click a hand slot to use it.\n\n## Layers\n`src/00-core` namespace B, rng, tuning. `10-12` rules, floors and text data. `20-25` the sim (pure, deterministic, JSON state, no view). `40-41` presenter (World3D). `50` audio. `60-66` UI. `70` Dev Mode. `71` attract. `72` walkthrough bot. `73` hub and Rat Run. `90-99` main, title, About.\nSee `CONTENT.md` for the data formats and `PATCHES.md` for engine changes.\n\n## What was cut from PLAN.md (honestly)\nSister Veil and her branch; the trapdoor; pen-drawn leech, spider, hound and rat knot (they are rig cards); the beard patch for dwarves; the engine's audio bus and panned sfx patches; 13 spells instead of 18; 15 monster types; the optional minimap; Settings \"Level up on rest\" is wired but only applied at rest. Every system the plan lists as required exists.\nEOF\ncat > CONTENT.md <<'EOF'\n# Content formats\n\n**Floors** (`src/11-data-floors.js`): `B.buildFloor({ w, h, rooms: [[x0,y0,x1,y1]...], set: { 'x,y': ch } ... })`. Cells: `#` wall, `.` floor, `+` door, `=` gate (named in `gates`), `L` locked door (`locks`), `M` magic seal, `H` secret wall, `I` illusory wall, `P` plate (`plates`), `T` dart trap, `O` pit (`pits`), `^` teleporter (`tele`), `S` spinner, `<` `>` stairs (`stairs`).\n**Wall features** are `{ at: [x, y, 'N'|'E'|'S'|'W'], k, id }` addressed by the open cell you stand in and the way you face: `lever`, `button`, `catch`, `alcove` (`holds`, `accepts`), `plaque` (`text` = id in `B.NOTES`), `candle`, `clock`, `undergate`, `greatLock`, `shrine`, `torch`.\n**Wires**: `{ when: 'lever:id:on' | 'plate:id:down' | 'catch:id' | 'alcove:id:in' | 'clock:whole' | 'seq:name:ok' | 'ug:open' | 'enter:x,y', do: [['gate', id, 'open'], ['secret', 'x,y'], ['special', 'd1'], ['msg', text], ['tele', id, 'off'], ['hurt', n], ['reset', seq]] }`.\n**Items / monsters / spells / classes**: `src/10-data-rules.js`. **Text**: `src/12-data-text.js`. **Tuning**: `B.TUNE` in `src/00-core.js` (the Dev Mode sliders). `node tests/lint.mjs` checks every map and id.\nEOF\ncat >> PATCHES.md <<'EOF'\n3. **Hub rule** (game code, not the engine): `game.pause` is wrapped so Options is ignored while Create is held in a session.\n4. The build escapes `</script` and `<!--` inside the inlined engine files: the 3D engine's header comment contains `</script>` text, which ended the inline script early.\nNot done (planned, cut): `E.Humanoid` beards, `audio.bus(name)`, `sfx(name, { pan })`.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs && timeout 120 node tests/browser.mjs","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2762,"cache_read_input_tokens":559665,"cache_creation":{"