{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghHExzSjN4PsFo3AL9oR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything TASK.md asks for is implemented and was checked against its feature list, and the last full suite run came after the final edit. Of the items I cut, only the \"beards\" and \"audio.bus\" engine patches are things TASK.md might arguably cover; the rest are `PLAN.md`-only.\n\n**TASK.md feature list, each with its evidence**\n- **Single HTML file:** it is in the root and boots from `file://`; the browser suite loads it.\n- **Genre and perspective:** a first-person party crawler with an automap; the browser suite plays it.\n- **Built on the handoff:** the engine and the 3D engine are inlined. One small engine patch (the Button symbols setting).\n- **Art, animation and audio in code:** no audio files; the voices use a babble synth. A voice-synth test and the browser suite cover it.\n- **Hub multiplayer:** the harness passes `players=2`, `players=4` with latency, jitter and loss, and `host-leave`. The ghost race and the solo best-run ghost are in the game.\n- **Dev mode with sliders:** live Tuning sliders, a Reset row, cheats, warp, party, spawn and debug tabs. The browser suite opens it and checks that Reset restores the defaults.\n- **Attract mode:** it starts after 10 s idle, not at 9.5 s, runs all its scenes with no errors, and any input exits. This is tested on desktop and on a touch-only device.\n- **10-foot controller-first UI:** PlayStation glyphs, Xbox in Settings, and prompts that follow the last device. The suite checks the PlayStation, Xbox and keyboard labels.\n- **Touch-only devices:** the \"Controller or keyboard required\" notice shows, with no touch controls.\n- **Narrative tone:** terse second-person writing in the source's style.\n- **Complete demo:** four floors plus the Rat Run, and every system works. A bot plays New Game to the ending with no cheats through all of them.\n- **No stubs:** I read `src/` for dead menu entries as well as grepping it; there are none and no TODO, FIXME or placeholder.\n\n**What was cut.** Sister Veil's branch, the trapdoor, pen-drawn spider/hound/leech (they are rig cards), 5 of the 18 planned spells (13 are in), the minimap (`PLAN.md` marks it optional), dwarf beards, and the audio-bus and panned-sfx patches.\n\n**Test coverage.** The full suite ran after the last source edit (the touch-notice and version-label fix, then a rebuild): 148 passed, 0 failed across 4 suites. The suite's playthrough runs seeds 7 and 21, and both pass. I also tried four more seeds by hand; two pass and two lose to the boss. A naive bot that never dodges wins about two thirds of the time, and I left the boss at that difficulty on purpose.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 20:26:13\n- **Source:** Eye of the Beholder (Westwood Associates / SSI, 1991; MS-DOS and Amiga)\n- **Plan:** `PLAN.md`\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Real-time, first-person, grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler. First-person party view on a grid with tweened steps and quarter turns, plus a top-down automap.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and my-3D2dge 3D v0.85.2 (three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3 via jsDelivr); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests; plain JavaScript in one HTML file.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native retro-modern look: code-drawn low-res 3D (pixel resolution, toon light, outlines, fog), rigs as pixel-art cards, procedural textures, pen-drawn mechanisms and boss, a brass \"lockwork\" UI.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs and moves, a tweened first-person camera, pen-animated mechanisms and the Bolt-Holder, telegraphed monster wind-ups and first-person weapon swings.\n- **Audio:** The engine's chip synth (step-sequencer songs with a combat layer, stings, sfx) plus a custom WebAudio formant babble voice synth. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1 to 4 players (the Rat Run); a solo time trial against your best-run ghost.\n- **Testing:** Node `vm` sim tests, content lint, a scripted playthrough bot, Playwright browser checks and the AI Hub harness; screenshots only for what scripts cannot judge; no subagents.\n- **Research:** Planning research from `PLAN.md`; engine docs and the crawler kit read in the build.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in headless Chromium).\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 15, among them the engine header's `</script>` text breaking the inlined bundle, font symbols that don't exist, a fixed per-world light limit, module-scope name clashes, bot soft-locks, door-versus-pickup conflicts, a non-modal dialogue freezing game time in attract mode, slow-frame-rate hub reporting, and three balance faults.\n- **Critical:** Six: the broken bundle, light exhaustion on re-entering a floor, the boot crash, the attract freeze, the first-den wipe and the unwinnable boss.\n- **Most helpful:** The scripted full playthrough bot; browser checks driven by `game.advance()` were a close second.\n- **Least helpful:** Wall-clock screenshot and attract waits on the 4 fps software renderer.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** One small API gives scenes, input with glyphs, settings, saves, Dialog, a chip synth and a 3D world; deterministic `game.advance` makes testing easy.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `</script>` text in the 3D header, build-time-only lights, the small 5x7 font, and Esc being taken for pause.\n- **Had to build myself:** The whole party-RPG layer: deterministic sim, presenter, 10-foot focus UI, babble voices and the walkthrough bot.\n- **Hardest part:** Fitting a grid crawler to a free-body engine, and making secret walls match the baked walls.\n- **Changed in the engine:** One patch: Button symbols default to PlayStation, with only PlayStation and Xbox offered.\n- **One change I'd make:** A grid-crawler helper in the 3D engine, and a wider font character set.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** A clear target, ordered work, exact tests and hub rules, and useful data tables.\n- **Confusing:** The scale exceeds a medium-effort session, and the \"cut quantity, never a system\" rule conflicts with it.\n- **Hardest:** Scoping to a vertical slice with every system and a good balance on a slow renderer.\n- **Would change:** Add ranked must-haves and cuts per effort level, give one full reference floor with its walkthrough, and make some engine patches optional."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3404,"cache_read_input_tokens":596786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3404},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"73c17cbf-74a4-4b14-849a-cdf24a7788d3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:46:58.313Z","request_id":"req_011CghHExfrg8RTSKvb1VnsB"}
