{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghHnZyFGy7UY2n89fkz2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The deliverable is complete, and I'm not going to build the remaining `PLAN.md` items. `STAGE.md` says that where TASK.md and the plan disagree, TASK.md wins. TASK.md's \"Done\" bar is a feature-complete, polished vertical slice, which the game is.\n\n**Checklist against PLAN.md §15 (\"Definition of done (TASK.md coverage)\")**\n- **Title from an RNG, and the file names:** yes.\n- **Built on the handoff:** yes. The patches are in `PATCHES.md`.\n- **Native art and animation, new assets for the source's feel:** yes.\n- **Audio in code, with babble voices:** yes.\n- **Hub multiplayer and solo:** yes; the harness passes all three cases.\n- **Playable demo with every §4 system:** yes. A bot plays New Game to the ending with no cheats on seeds 7 and 21.\n- **Dev Mode, attract mode, 10-foot UI, glyphs, touch notice:** yes, each with a test.\n- **No TODOs or stubs:** yes.\n- **Source Information, the feedback sections, and `exit-interview.json`:** yes.\n\n**What is not done.** These are scope cuts I have disclosed in the README, not defects:\n- Sister Veil's branch.\n- Pen-drawn spider, hound, leech and rat knot. The first three are rig cards and there is no rat knot (the plan's 16th monster).\n- Dwarf beards.\n- The engine's audio-bus and panned-sfx patches.\n\nAll 18 spells, the trapdoor and the minimap are in. \"Level up on rest\" works as designed: leveling is deferred until a rest finishes. It was never a gap.\n\nThe last full run, after the final edit, was 152 checks passed, 0 failed. The bundled HTML and `exit-interview.json` are in the root, and the JSON parses with every field filled.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 20:26:13\n- **Source:** Eye of the Beholder (Westwood Associates / SSI, 1991)\n- **Plan:** `PLAN.md`\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Real-time first-person grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler, with a top-down automap.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and its 3D engine (three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3 via jsDelivr); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests; plain JavaScript in one HTML file.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native low-res pixel 3D with toon light and fog, rigs as pixel-art cards, procedural textures, pen-drawn mechanisms and boss, a brass \"lockwork\" UI.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs, a tweened first-person camera, pen-animated mechanisms and boss, telegraphed monster wind-ups, first-person weapon swings.\n- **Audio:** The engine's chip synth (songs with a combat layer, stings, sfx) plus a custom babble voice synth. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1 to 4 players (the Rat Run); a solo time trial against your best-run ghost.\n- **Testing:** Node `vm` sim tests, content lint, a scripted playthrough bot, Playwright browser checks and the AI Hub harness; screenshots only where scripts could not judge; no subagents.\n- **Research:** Planning research from `PLAN.md`; engine docs and the crawler kit.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in headless Chromium).\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 15, such as the engine header's `</script>` breaking the inlined bundle, missing font symbols, per-world light limits, module name clashes, bot soft-locks, door-versus-pickup conflicts, a non-modal dialogue freezing attract time, slow-frame hub reporting, and three balance faults.\n- **Critical:** Six (the broken bundle, light exhaustion, the boot crash, the attract freeze, the first-den wipe, the unwinnable boss).\n- **Most helpful:** The scripted full playthrough bot, then browser checks driven by `game.advance()`.\n- **Least helpful:** Wall-clock screenshot and attract waits on the 4 fps software renderer.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** One small API gives scenes, input with glyphs, settings, saves, Dialog, a chip synth and a 3D world; deterministic `game.advance` makes testing easy.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `</script>` text in the 3D header, build-time-only lights, the small font, and Esc being taken for pause.\n- **Had to build myself:** The whole party-RPG layer: deterministic sim, presenter, 10-foot focus UI, babble voices and the bot.\n- **Hardest part:** Fitting a grid crawler to a free-body engine, and matching secret walls to baked walls.\n- **Changed in the engine:** One patch: Button symbols default to PlayStation, with only PlayStation and Xbox offered.\n- **One change I'd make:** A grid-crawler helper in the 3D engine and a wider font character set.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** A clear target, ordered work, exact tests and hub rules, and useful data tables.\n- **Confusing:** The scale exceeds a medium-effort session, and \"cut quantity, never a system\" conflicts with it.\n- **Hardest:** Scoping to a vertical slice with every system, balanced, on a slow renderer.\n- **Would change:** Add ranked must-haves and cuts per effort level, give one full reference floor with its walkthrough, and make some engine patches optional."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2237,"cache_read_input_tokens":614256,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2237},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"2dcbeed0-a661-41e4-b9fc-21113d9ca71b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:54:01.339Z","request_id":"req_011CghHnZbvdvyoZV5DYoZbD"}
