{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghJMij1xHmudCUeTJTdk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked the build against PLAN §4's mechanics line by line this time, and it turned up gaps. The full suite passes with 157 checks and 0 failures, and the bundled HTML and `exit-interview.json` are still in the root.\n\n**Built and tested**\n- **Movement and puzzles (§4.1–4.2):**\n  - Tweened steps with buffering, bumps and stairs.\n  - Doors and gates, locked doors (keys are used up), and a thief picking simple locks.\n  - Magic seals, secret and illusory walls, plates (hold and latch; a rock on a plate works), dart traps, pits, trapdoors, teleporters (silent ones loop), spinners, levers, buttons, catches, alcoves, plaques, candle sequences, the clock, the Undergate and the Great Locks.\n  - The wiring language, escalating hints, and thief disarm of dart traps (added this round).\n- **Party and items (§4.3–4.5):** four races, six classes, formation rows and reach, character creation, paperdoll with equip rules, the Hand (take, stow, put down, throw), eating, potions and wands.\n- **Combat and monsters (§4.6–4.7):** per-hand cooldowns, Party Strike, flank targeting, telegraphed wind-ups that a step dodges, projectiles, statuses and the 16 monster types.\n- **Boss and magic (§4.7.4, §4.8):** the Bolt-Holder's three phases, its four attacks and its relock; all 18 spells, memorizing, scribing and scrolls.\n- **Camp and progress (§4.9–4.15):** rest, interruptions, safe rooms, food and starving, XP and levels, down, death, raising, game over, NPCs and Sister Veil, the journal, the automap with an optional minimap, and saves.\n- **Settings (§4.16), UI, hub, tests (§5–§14):** the settings listed there, UI and glyphs, Dev Mode, attract mode, touch notice, hub ghost race and the Rat Run, and the tests.\n\n**Not built from §4**\n- Lay on Hands (the paladin heal) and Turn the Dead (the cleric's turn-undead).\n- Brace gives the Defense bonus but no HUD cue beyond the cooldown.\n- The `warded` lock kind and the `buttons within N seconds` wire exist in the data language but no floor uses them.\n- The level-up setting only defers leveling until a rest.\n\nNone of these are TASK.md requirements, and every system TASK.md asks for is built and tested. No TODOs or placeholders remain in the code.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 20:26:13\n- **Source:** Eye of the Beholder (Westwood Associates / SSI, 1991)\n- **Plan:** `PLAN.md`\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Real-time first-person grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler, with a top-down automap.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and its 3D engine (three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3 via jsDelivr); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests; plain JavaScript in one HTML file.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native low-res pixel 3D with toon light and fog, rigs as pixel-art cards, procedural textures, pen-drawn mechanisms, creatures and boss, a brass \"lockwork\" UI.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs, a tweened first-person camera, pen-animated mechanisms and creatures, telegraphed monster wind-ups, first-person weapon swings.\n- **Audio:** The engine's chip synth (songs with a combat layer, stings, panned sfx) plus a custom babble voice synth on a voice bus. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1 to 4 players (the Rat Run); a solo time trial against your best-run ghost.\n- **Testing:** Node `vm` sim tests, content lint, a scripted playthrough bot, Playwright browser checks and the AI Hub harness; screenshots only where scripts could not judge; no subagents.\n- **Research:** Planning research from `PLAN.md`; engine docs and the crawler kit.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in headless Chromium).\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 15, such as the engine header's `</script>` breaking the inlined bundle, missing font symbols, per-world light limits, module name clashes, bot soft-locks, door-versus-pickup conflicts, a non-modal dialogue freezing attract time, slow-frame hub reporting, and three balance faults.\n- **Critical:** Six (the broken bundle, light exhaustion, the boot crash, the attract freeze, the first-den wipe, the unwinnable boss).\n- **Most helpful:** The scripted full playthrough bot, then browser checks driven by `game.advance()`.\n- **Least helpful:** Wall-clock screenshot and attract waits on the 4 fps software renderer.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** One small API gives scenes, input with glyphs, settings, saves, Dialog, a chip synth and a 3D world; deterministic `game.advance` makes testing easy.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `</script>` text in the 3D header, build-time-only lights, the small font, and Esc being taken for pause.\n- **Had to build myself:** The whole party-RPG layer: deterministic sim, presenter, 10-foot focus UI, babble voices and the bot.\n- **Hardest part:** Fitting a grid crawler to a free-body engine, and matching secret walls to baked walls.\n- **Changed in the engine:** Two small patches: Button symbols default to PlayStation (PlayStation and Xbox only), and audio gained `bus(name)` and `sfx(name, { pan })`.\n- **One change I'd make:** A grid-crawler helper in the 3D engine and a wider font character set.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** A clear target, ordered work, exact tests and hub rules, and useful data tables.\n- **Confusing:** The scale exceeds a medium-effort session, and \"cut quantity, never a system\" conflicts with it.\n- **Hardest:** Scoping to a vertical slice with every system, balanced, on a slow renderer.\n- **Would change:** Add ranked must-haves and cuts per effort level, give one full reference floor with its walkthrough, and make some engine patches optional."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1296,"cache_read_input_tokens":637598,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1296},"output_tokens":798,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"2e81dfee-c29d-43e8-89fa-5244c5083757","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:01:44.371Z","request_id":"req_011CghJMiQffQwCRH8YSRhyJ"}
