{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghJr6p65Ss1jtnzcsvPg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are TASK.md's own words next to the test or screenshot behind each one. The run behind this is the one just completed: 163 passed, 0 failed across 4 suites.\n\n| TASK.md, verbatim | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| \"provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-202613].html\" | `EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-202613.html` is in the root. The browser suite boots it from `file://` with no console errors. |\n| \"Include a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu ... expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\" | The pause menu lists Dev Mode. 22 sliders sit in Tuning with a Reset row. Browser check \"Reset to defaults restores sliders\" passes, and `shots/dev.png` shows the screen. |\n| \"After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo ... any input exits it.\" | Browser checks \"attract not started at 9.5 s\", \"attract starts after 10 s idle\", \"attract runs with no errors\", \"attract visits several floors\" and \"any key exits the attract mode\" all pass. |\n| \"Follow ... ai-hub/lib/hub for multiplayer ... as well as for the game on its own.\" | The harness passes all three cases. The Rat Run also runs solo against your best ghost; the browser suite checks that it starts. |\n| \"PS5 DualSense ... PlayStation glyphs ... with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs\" | Browser checks: the use prompt is ✕ on a pad, A with the Xbox setting, and F on the keyboard. |\n| \"Touch-only devices: no touch controls; show 'Controller or keyboard required' and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\" | Browser checks \"touch-only: the notice shows\" and \"touch-only: attract mode runs\" pass. `shots/touch.png` shows the notice. |\n| \"Narrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source's\" | The writing is terse second-person text, for example \"You can't go that way.\" and \"The Drains keep what they take.\" |\n| \"All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files.\" | The audio is the chip synth plus a babble voice synth, and no audio file is in the bundle. The sim suite checks the babble output. |\n| \"demo must be long enough to show ALL features\" | A bot plays New Game to the ending with no cheats on seeds 7 and 21. Both pass in under 90 minutes, with no wipe. |\n| \"No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features\" | I grepped `src/` and the build tool for TODO, FIXME, placeholder, stub, \"not implemented\" and \"coming soon\" and got 0 hits. Every menu entry runs. |\n| \"Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen.\" | The sections are below, and the About screen shows them (`shots/about.png`). |\n| \"save these answers as exit-interview.json ... check that the file parses as JSON\" | It is in the root, parses, and has every field filled. |\n\nI have not run the whole `PLAN.md` feature list line by line a third time. TASK.md's checklist above is complete, and `STAGE.md` says TASK.md wins where the two disagree.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 20:26:13\n- **Source:** Eye of the Beholder (Westwood Associates / SSI, 1991)\n- **Plan:** `PLAN.md`\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Real-time first-person grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler, with a top-down automap.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and its 3D engine (three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3 via jsDelivr); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests; plain JavaScript in one HTML file.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native low-res pixel 3D with toon light and fog, rigs as pixel-art cards, procedural textures, pen-drawn mechanisms, creatures and boss, a brass \"lockwork\" UI.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs, a tweened first-person camera, pen-animated mechanisms and creatures, telegraphed monster wind-ups, first-person weapon swings.\n- **Audio:** The engine's chip synth (songs with a combat layer, stings, panned sfx) plus a custom babble voice synth on a voice bus. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1 to 4 players (the Rat Run); a solo time trial against your best-run ghost.\n- **Testing:** Node `vm` sim tests, content lint, a scripted playthrough bot, Playwright browser checks and the AI Hub harness; screenshots only where scripts could not judge; no subagents.\n- **Research:** Planning research from `PLAN.md`; engine docs and the crawler kit.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in headless Chromium).\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 15, such as the engine header's `</script>` breaking the inlined bundle, missing font symbols, per-world light limits, module name clashes, bot soft-locks, door-versus-pickup conflicts, a non-modal dialogue freezing attract time, slow-frame hub reporting, and three balance faults.\n- **Critical:** Six (the broken bundle, light exhaustion, the boot crash, the attract freeze, the first-den wipe, the unwinnable boss).\n- **Most helpful:** The scripted full playthrough bot, then browser checks driven by `game.advance()`.\n- **Least helpful:** Wall-clock screenshot and attract waits on the 4 fps software renderer.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** One small API gives scenes, input with glyphs, settings, saves, Dialog, a chip synth and a 3D world; deterministic `game.advance` makes testing easy.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** `</script>` text in the 3D header, build-time-only lights, the small font, and Esc being taken for pause.\n- **Had to build myself:** The whole party-RPG layer: deterministic sim, presenter, 10-foot focus UI, babble voices and the bot.\n- **Hardest part:** Fitting a grid crawler to a free-body engine, and matching secret walls to baked walls.\n- **Changed in the engine:** Two small patches: Button symbols default to PlayStation (PlayStation and Xbox only), and audio gained `bus(name)` and `sfx(name, { pan })`.\n- **One change I'd make:** A grid-crawler helper in the 3D engine and a wider font character set.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** A clear target, ordered work, exact tests and hub rules, and useful data tables.\n- **Confusing:** The scale exceeds a medium-effort session, and \"cut quantity, never a system\" conflicts with it.\n- **Hardest:** Scoping to a vertical slice with every system, balanced, on a slow renderer.\n- **Would change:** Add ranked must-haves and cuts per effort level, give one full reference floor with its walkthrough, and make some engine patches optional."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2102,"cache_read_input_tokens":662012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2102},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c69a81a-1298-4714-b95d-17fe664f547a","uuid":"dda0eb6d-e275-489c-b668-7816de1b724a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:07:57.379Z","request_id":"req_011CghJr6SmLWxQZvC6pG1CD"}
